[1m[38;5;231mWhat should the username field policy be?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mpresence (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mRecords whether a username was supplied, never its value. No PII reaches the log store. Cost: you can't tell which
[39m     [38;5;246maccount hit a bug from logs alone.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m raw
     [38;5;246mLog the actual username. Makes 'user X can't log in' directly answerable, which is a very common support need. [39m
     [38;5;246mCost: PII in your log store, with the retention and access-control obligations that brings.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m length
     [38;5;246mRecords only the character count. Catches whitespace/truncation/encoding bugs without storing identity; useless for
[39m     [38;5;246mcorrelating with a specific user report.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
